    "body": "## Summary\n- add a bounded per-account rate limiter for provider-backed routing operations\n- weight requests by actual provider-call cost (`POST /routing/quotes` = 1, mode estimates = 2)\n- return `429` + `Retry-After` without exposing account or location data\n- wire production configuration and Compose defaults\n- add unit coverage and operational/security documentation\n\n## Why\nAuthenticated routing requests can invoke the paid Google Routes provider. Existing auth and ownership controls prevent unauthorized access but did not bound provider cost/resource exhaustion for a valid account.\n\n## Validation\n- API/Maven verify via CI\n- frontend tests/audit/lint/build via CI\n- production Compose contract via CI\n- container/runtime smokes via CI\n\nNo Flyway migration is required because the limiter uses bounded ephemeral per-instance state.",
